1
00:00:19,916 --> 00:00:20,959
Next, please.

2
00:00:21,042 --> 00:00:21,876
‎JUNKO TAMAI - MINISTRY OF FINANCE

3
00:00:33,304 --> 00:00:35,682
Mo… Mori!

4
00:00:46,484 --> 00:00:47,819
MORI MACHI - CUSTOMS

5
00:00:50,071 --> 00:00:50,905
What?

6
00:00:59,205 --> 00:01:01,875
IMMIGRATION OFFICER (MINISTRY OF JUSTICE)
KEIICHIRO HAYAMI

7
00:01:03,376 --> 00:01:04,544
‎What?

8
00:01:21,853 --> 00:01:23,104
<i>I keep telling you.</i>

9
00:01:23,188 --> 00:01:26,357
Stick to inspection procedures.
Don't do unnecessary things.

10
00:01:26,441 --> 00:01:27,358
‎Yes…

11
00:01:27,442 --> 00:01:30,945
Mori, whenever something catches your eye,
you hyper-focus on it, don't you?

12
00:01:31,029 --> 00:01:33,156
And everything else
goes completely out of focus.

13
00:01:33,239 --> 00:01:34,824
Have you always been like that?

14
00:01:34,908 --> 00:01:37,869
Yes. I used to get scolded
at my previous job too.

15
00:01:37,952 --> 00:01:39,203
-Your previous job?
-Yes.

16
00:01:39,287 --> 00:01:42,749
-Come to think of it, where did you--
-Everyone, look!

17
00:01:42,832 --> 00:01:46,377
Ta-da! Tickets
to the Hi-Fi Unicorn concert!

18
00:01:46,461 --> 00:01:48,504
Amazing! You got Hi-Fi tickets?

19
00:01:48,588 --> 00:01:50,840
So Tamai missed out on the Hi-Fi tickets?

20
00:01:50,924 --> 00:01:54,510
-Don't mention that.
-Hi-Fi's coming to Japan today.

21
00:01:55,261 --> 00:01:56,846
Um…

22
00:01:58,014 --> 00:02:00,475
What is Hi-Fi?

23
00:02:00,558 --> 00:02:01,976
‎What?

24
00:02:02,769 --> 00:02:04,312
-You don't know Hi-Fi?
-No.

25
00:02:04,395 --> 00:02:06,064
You know, the ones who hold the fans.

26
00:02:06,147 --> 00:02:07,232
‎Look.

27
00:02:08,441 --> 00:02:13,404
Hi-Fi Unicorn.
A TJ Produced Korean idol group.

28
00:02:13,488 --> 00:02:15,448
It's their first Japan tour in a year.

29
00:02:15,531 --> 00:02:17,283
They set off fireworks
at their concerts, right?

30
00:02:17,367 --> 00:02:19,494
Just seeing that would make me so happy.

31
00:02:20,328 --> 00:02:22,205
8:30. I won't be able to make it…

32
00:02:22,288 --> 00:02:25,458
They're world-famous, look.

33
00:02:31,047 --> 00:02:32,423
You all know a lot about them.

34
00:02:32,507 --> 00:02:35,260
More like, how does a walking encyclopedia
like you not know about them?

35
00:02:35,343 --> 00:02:37,428
Ah, I don't know much about recent stuff.

36
00:02:38,054 --> 00:02:41,808
Won't they be passing through your gate?

37
00:02:41,891 --> 00:02:44,519
-Can you get me an autograph?
-Absolutely not.

38
00:02:44,602 --> 00:02:46,145
Work is work.

39
00:02:46,229 --> 00:02:49,190
First of all, VIPs have a dedicated route,
so they won't be coming to us.

40
00:02:49,273 --> 00:02:51,526
Where's the romance?

41
00:02:51,609 --> 00:02:53,194
If you want romance, go watch their show.

42
00:02:53,778 --> 00:02:56,990
-That's a good one!
-Right, right.

43
00:03:04,455 --> 00:03:06,541
Um…

44
00:03:06,624 --> 00:03:09,544
Hayami, thank you for earlier.

45
00:03:10,670 --> 00:03:11,754
It's nothing.

46
00:03:15,591 --> 00:03:16,634
Um, Mori…

47
00:03:18,219 --> 00:03:19,762
What was your previous job?

48
00:03:20,638 --> 00:03:22,473
-Um…
-This is terrible!

49
00:03:23,474 --> 00:03:28,062
This is terrible! There's
a system failure on the VIP route.

50
00:03:28,813 --> 00:03:31,274
-What?
-What about Hi-Fi's entry procedures?

51
00:03:31,357 --> 00:03:33,484
The only booths available right now are…

52
00:03:47,373 --> 00:03:49,876
-Please step back, for your safety.
-Please step back!

53
00:03:51,294 --> 00:03:54,213
-It's not safe.
-Clear the way!

54
00:03:54,297 --> 00:03:57,258
Why are there fans here?

55
00:03:57,342 --> 00:03:59,177
-They're from the same flight.
-Please step back!

56
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:02,972
We asked them to wait
so we could let you all through first.

57
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:16,903
‎HI-FI UN!CORN - BOY BAND

58
00:04:16,986 --> 00:04:18,404
It's really them.

59
00:04:19,197 --> 00:04:22,408
This is Hi-Fi Unicorn.

60
00:04:23,117 --> 00:04:25,328
Work. This is work.

61
00:04:26,371 --> 00:04:29,040
What are we waiting for? Hurry it up.

62
00:04:29,123 --> 00:04:30,541
I'm very sorry.

63
00:04:30,625 --> 00:04:31,501
What?

64
00:04:32,168 --> 00:04:33,252
Their concert is soon.

65
00:04:33,336 --> 00:04:35,963
-Please speed up the entry procedures.
-Yes.

66
00:04:36,047 --> 00:04:36,881
Can I go?

67
00:04:38,216 --> 00:04:39,050
‎This way, please.

68
00:04:40,385 --> 00:04:41,928
‎Please wait a moment.

69
00:04:42,011 --> 00:04:44,222
-Passport, please.
-Everyone, please wait a little longer!

70
00:04:44,305 --> 00:04:47,266
This time it's mainly
identity verification.

71
00:04:47,350 --> 00:04:49,852
-It shouldn't take long.
-Yes.

72
00:04:49,936 --> 00:04:51,896
I never expected things
to turn out like this.

73
00:04:51,979 --> 00:04:55,191
Handling the unexpected
is what Gate 24 is all about.

74
00:04:55,274 --> 00:04:56,401
Go ahead.

75
00:05:01,989 --> 00:05:04,075
Everything is in order. Welcome to Japan.

76
00:05:10,206 --> 00:05:12,333
Tamai is in full work mode.

77
00:05:13,209 --> 00:05:15,169
Her fangirl mode
is completely sealed away.

78
00:05:16,295 --> 00:05:17,255
Okay.

79
00:05:26,597 --> 00:05:28,433
What's wrong, Hyeongyul?

80
00:05:28,516 --> 00:05:31,018
I think I left my passport somewhere.

81
00:05:31,644 --> 00:05:32,770
Calm down and look for it.

82
00:05:32,854 --> 00:05:34,272
Okay.

83
00:05:35,481 --> 00:05:36,649
Let me help you.

84
00:05:38,651 --> 00:05:39,902
-Thank you very much.
-It's okay.

85
00:05:43,990 --> 00:05:45,158
Thank you.

86
00:05:50,955 --> 00:05:52,832
Mori, stop that already.

87
00:06:01,883 --> 00:06:03,509
Machi Mori?

88
00:06:06,262 --> 00:06:08,931
I thought it was you! It's me, Yuki.

89
00:06:12,685 --> 00:06:13,644
Miss Yuki.

90
00:06:15,479 --> 00:06:16,522
‎Yes.

91
00:06:17,106 --> 00:06:20,776
Miss Yuki! It's me, Chika!

92
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:22,570
-Kumagawa?
-Yes!

93
00:06:22,653 --> 00:06:24,780
Do you know each other?

94
00:06:25,615 --> 00:06:27,992
I used to teach at a Japanese school.
They were my students.

95
00:06:28,075 --> 00:06:29,952
What a wonderful coincidence.

96
00:06:30,036 --> 00:06:32,914
We're basically Yuki's students too.

97
00:06:32,997 --> 00:06:34,040
So we're friends!

98
00:06:34,123 --> 00:06:36,709
-Friends, friends.
-Friends…

99
00:06:38,794 --> 00:06:40,922
Wow, I'm so jealous.

100
00:06:41,923 --> 00:06:45,051
-Wait, Mori, you lived overseas?
-Yes.

101
00:06:45,134 --> 00:06:47,053
I didn't expect to meet you here.

102
00:06:47,803 --> 00:06:49,347
It's been a long time, Miss Yuki.

103
00:06:50,264 --> 00:06:52,934
-I'm a manager now.
-Yuki.

104
00:06:54,352 --> 00:06:55,686
Yes.

105
00:06:55,770 --> 00:06:57,438
Hyeongyul, where is your passport?

106
00:06:58,022 --> 00:06:59,065
The thing is…

107
00:07:05,488 --> 00:07:06,697
He doesn't have his passport?

108
00:07:08,157 --> 00:07:09,075
Okay!

109
00:07:09,742 --> 00:07:10,952
You don't have it?

110
00:07:11,953 --> 00:07:13,246
Look for it carefully.

111
00:07:13,329 --> 00:07:15,456
Is someone holding it for him?

112
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:16,832
For now, send them
to secondary inspection.

113
00:07:16,916 --> 00:07:19,418
Have the ones waiting go ahead.

114
00:07:19,502 --> 00:07:20,336
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

115
00:07:21,462 --> 00:07:23,297
Please guide the passengers.

116
00:07:23,381 --> 00:07:24,924
Everyone, please step
this way for a moment.

117
00:07:25,007 --> 00:07:25,925
‎Yes, sir.

118
00:07:26,008 --> 00:07:28,844
Wait! He's the real Hyeongyul.

119
00:07:28,928 --> 00:07:31,097
Just let him through!

120
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:32,848
-President…
-Shut up.

121
00:07:32,932 --> 00:07:37,061
I'm very sorry, but no matter who it is,
we cannot permit entry without a passport.

122
00:07:37,144 --> 00:07:39,313
We perform at six p.m.

123
00:07:39,397 --> 00:07:41,857
Who's going to take
responsibility if we don't make it?

124
00:07:41,941 --> 00:07:42,984
Will you?

125
00:07:44,402 --> 00:07:46,612
-Don't you know Hi-Fi?
-You can come this way too.

126
00:07:46,696 --> 00:07:50,658
We'll give you the document later, okay?

127
00:07:50,741 --> 00:07:53,160
Just let him through. Please.

128
00:07:55,246 --> 00:07:57,748
-So?
-He dropped it in the walkway.

129
00:07:58,666 --> 00:08:00,001
The walkway?

130
00:08:00,668 --> 00:08:02,753
I dropped my bag.

131
00:08:03,713 --> 00:08:05,381
Hyeongyul!

132
00:08:07,049 --> 00:08:08,676
<i>Could I have dropped it then?</i>

133
00:08:12,263 --> 00:08:13,598
No passports in the walkway.

134
00:08:15,474 --> 00:08:17,643
So maybe someone picked it up.

135
00:08:20,187 --> 00:08:23,399
Which means…

136
00:08:27,903 --> 00:08:30,239
It's someone among them?

137
00:08:38,247 --> 00:08:39,665
Oh my.

138
00:08:47,089 --> 00:08:50,259
I hear the VIP processing
has ground to a halt.

139
00:08:51,594 --> 00:08:53,721
And of all places, they're at Gate 24!

140
00:08:53,804 --> 00:08:56,015
-Of all places?
-Ah, no…

141
00:08:56,098 --> 00:09:00,770
This Japanese concert tour is part
of a cultural exchange effort with Korea.

142
00:09:00,853 --> 00:09:02,480
Overseas media have their eyes on it.

143
00:09:03,272 --> 00:09:04,315
The scale is in the hundreds of millions.

144
00:09:04,398 --> 00:09:08,277
If the show gets disrupted, it becomes
a major diplomatic and economic issue.

145
00:09:08,361 --> 00:09:09,820
Are you at least aware of that?

146
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:13,115
Anyway, just take care of it.

147
00:09:13,199 --> 00:09:14,241
‎TAKAHIRO IKEURA
‎DIRECTOR OF KANTO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

148
00:09:18,329 --> 00:09:20,539
-Please handle things on the floor.
-Yes.

149
00:09:23,959 --> 00:09:25,878
To all inspection booths.

150
00:09:25,961 --> 00:09:29,340
There is a possibility that a passenger
picked up the missing passport.

151
00:09:29,423 --> 00:09:32,468
<i>Please politely check</i>
<i>with passengers at each booth.</i>

152
00:09:32,551 --> 00:09:33,552
Roger that.

153
00:09:35,471 --> 00:09:37,306
-Tamai.
-Step here, please.

154
00:09:37,390 --> 00:09:39,100
Let's continue inspecting.

155
00:09:39,183 --> 00:09:40,101
Yes.

156
00:09:40,184 --> 00:09:41,686
IMMIGRATION TICKET EXAMINATION SYSTEM

157
00:10:09,046 --> 00:10:11,632
-A camera, a telephoto lens.
-Yes.

158
00:10:16,303 --> 00:10:17,805
Step here, please.

159
00:10:17,888 --> 00:10:19,765
I'll check your passport.

160
00:10:29,150 --> 00:10:30,276
Mira Tono, right?

161
00:10:31,193 --> 00:10:33,237
You're returning from South Korea, right?

162
00:10:33,904 --> 00:10:35,364
I live over there permanently.

163
00:10:37,742 --> 00:10:38,784
Welcome back.

164
00:10:41,495 --> 00:10:42,538
Is something wrong?

165
00:10:51,005 --> 00:10:52,631
MIRA TONO

166
00:10:52,715 --> 00:10:54,717
PORTRAIT
FINGERPRINTS

167
00:11:13,736 --> 00:11:18,574
You know, food this good is always better
when you share it with someone.

168
00:11:18,657 --> 00:11:20,201
So, wanna try some?

169
00:11:21,452 --> 00:11:23,454
You can't bring that into Japan.

170
00:11:24,497 --> 00:11:25,372
Oh, really?

171
00:11:26,290 --> 00:11:28,209
-He's got a lot more!
-What?

172
00:11:28,292 --> 00:11:32,755
Bacon, salami, sausage…
These are all not allowed.

173
00:11:32,838 --> 00:11:35,132
All of them? Wow.

174
00:11:35,841 --> 00:11:38,385
That's impressive.

175
00:11:43,891 --> 00:11:45,559
MIRA TONO

176
00:11:45,643 --> 00:11:48,103
Excuse me, ma'am, about this…

177
00:11:49,522 --> 00:11:50,523
I had plastic surgery.

178
00:11:53,150 --> 00:11:54,944
Do you have
a post-operative certificate or…

179
00:11:55,027 --> 00:11:57,947
No, the surgery was about a year ago.

180
00:12:00,783 --> 00:12:03,786
-Then at exit control, how did--
-I just told them I used lots of makeup.

181
00:12:05,955 --> 00:12:08,666
Departure control is pretty lenient
in most countries.

182
00:12:09,875 --> 00:12:13,754
If we cannot verify that you
are the passport holder,

183
00:12:13,837 --> 00:12:16,507
-we cannot grant you entry.
-What?

184
00:12:16,590 --> 00:12:18,842
The Hi-Fi concert is tonight.
Let me through!

185
00:12:18,926 --> 00:12:21,637
-Oh, uh, well…
-Hey!

186
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:23,806
-Hurry it up!
-Um, okay, uh…

187
00:12:23,889 --> 00:12:25,558
Um, please wait a moment.

188
00:12:29,770 --> 00:12:31,772
Why is everyone getting
let through except me?

189
00:12:31,855 --> 00:12:34,191
You are right, but, um…

190
00:12:34,275 --> 00:12:36,360
The surgery… Ah, excuse me.

191
00:12:37,236 --> 00:12:40,114
Well, you see…

192
00:12:40,197 --> 00:12:41,323
you've had surgery, but…

193
00:12:47,955 --> 00:12:50,499
Crazy day.

194
00:12:50,583 --> 00:12:52,167
It's just one thing after another.

195
00:12:55,087 --> 00:12:56,130
What should we do?

196
00:13:00,134 --> 00:13:01,427
Knew you'd say that.

197
00:13:01,510 --> 00:13:04,346
Or so I'd like to say.

198
00:13:05,639 --> 00:13:08,183
But I think we all need
to help deal with this problem.

199
00:13:08,767 --> 00:13:10,978
It's rare for you to say
something like that, Hayami.

200
00:13:13,230 --> 00:13:14,940
I just want to get this over with.

201
00:13:18,068 --> 00:13:19,987
This is the last passenger.

202
00:13:20,863 --> 00:13:22,239
Your passport, please.

203
00:13:25,534 --> 00:13:26,619
THREE-WAY IMMIGRATION
PASSPORT READING SYSTEM

204
00:13:26,702 --> 00:13:28,162
HAORU

205
00:13:28,245 --> 00:13:31,790
Rensi Haoru, correct?
What is the purpose of your visit?

206
00:13:33,083 --> 00:13:34,376
I have no idea.

207
00:13:35,586 --> 00:13:38,839
-Pardon?
-Is this Japan?

208
00:13:39,590 --> 00:13:41,842
-Yes.
-Let me think a little…

209
00:13:41,925 --> 00:13:43,969
This is Kanto International Airport.

210
00:13:44,053 --> 00:13:46,555
Why am I here?

211
00:14:02,071 --> 00:14:04,239
It might be stress-induced amnesia.

212
00:14:04,323 --> 00:14:05,783
Amnesia.

213
00:14:06,408 --> 00:14:09,119
A condition where
a portion of memory is lost.

214
00:14:10,913 --> 00:14:13,707
His vital signs are stable,
so let's observe him for a while.

215
00:14:14,583 --> 00:14:15,834
Okay.

216
00:14:15,918 --> 00:14:18,837
I'm sorry. Would it be all right
if he stays here with you all as well?

217
00:14:18,921 --> 00:14:21,340
-Of course.
-Are you all right, sir?

218
00:14:22,675 --> 00:14:23,801
Are you all right?

219
00:14:29,348 --> 00:14:32,893
Um… Are you feeling okay?

220
00:14:33,894 --> 00:14:35,896
-What?
-Do you have a fever?

221
00:14:37,648 --> 00:14:39,066
Do you feel unwell at all?

222
00:14:39,149 --> 00:14:42,611
Of course he's okay.

223
00:14:42,695 --> 00:14:44,113
He's a professional, isn't he?

224
00:14:44,196 --> 00:14:46,156
-Yes, there's no problem.
-See?

225
00:14:47,074 --> 00:14:49,118
-He seems fine.
-But…

226
00:14:52,454 --> 00:14:55,457
Doctor, could you examine him
as well, just to be safe?

227
00:14:55,541 --> 00:14:57,042
Sure.

228
00:14:59,837 --> 00:15:01,755
Hey, we don't have time for this.

229
00:15:01,839 --> 00:15:04,091
-Just your arm, please.
-You four head to the venue first.

230
00:15:04,174 --> 00:15:07,678
-No, we'll wait here as long as possible.
-What?

231
00:15:07,761 --> 00:15:10,597
We want all five of us
to stand on stage together.

232
00:15:10,681 --> 00:15:12,307
-Yeah.
-Please, President.

233
00:15:16,687 --> 00:15:18,856
Yuki, do you have a moment?

234
00:15:23,527 --> 00:15:25,279
Provisional landing permission?

235
00:15:25,362 --> 00:15:26,780
Yes. However,

236
00:15:27,573 --> 00:15:32,494
it depends on whether the embassy
can issue a passport during their stay.

237
00:15:37,249 --> 00:15:40,753
Please let us know your contact info
and place of stay in Japan.

238
00:15:41,420 --> 00:15:43,881
I'll ask MOFA
how his visa will be handled.

239
00:15:43,964 --> 00:15:44,923
Thank you.

240
00:15:45,007 --> 00:15:46,133
Can you fill this out?

241
00:15:47,134 --> 00:15:47,968
Hello?

242
00:15:51,722 --> 00:15:53,348
Is everything okay there?

243
00:15:54,767 --> 00:15:58,479
Um… That pouch…

244
00:15:58,562 --> 00:16:01,315
This? It's official Hi-Fi merch.

245
00:16:01,398 --> 00:16:03,150
-Interested?
-Yes.

246
00:16:03,233 --> 00:16:05,152
The fans had them too.

247
00:16:06,070 --> 00:16:09,740
-And…
-Mori, you really like objects, huh?

248
00:16:10,866 --> 00:16:11,992
You were like that back then, too.

249
00:16:13,660 --> 00:16:14,995
Back then?

250
00:16:16,163 --> 00:16:20,459
<i>Mother crow, why do you squawk so?</i>

251
00:16:20,542 --> 00:16:24,797
<i>Because high on the mountain</i>

252
00:16:24,880 --> 00:16:26,006
<i>I have seven cute…</i>

253
00:16:26,090 --> 00:16:27,382
Stop.

254
00:16:28,008 --> 00:16:29,468
Mori, what are you doing?

255
00:16:31,929 --> 00:16:33,806
Machi, you're reading again!

256
00:16:34,973 --> 00:16:36,517
Chika, it's okay.

257
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:39,061
ENCYCLOPEDIA

258
00:16:41,355 --> 00:16:42,523
Do you like encyclopedias?

259
00:16:43,482 --> 00:16:45,317
Your father's a scholar, right?

260
00:16:47,778 --> 00:16:49,530
Would you like to sing with everyone?

261
00:16:50,531 --> 00:16:53,283
All your fellow Japanese friends
are gathered here.

262
00:16:53,367 --> 00:16:55,119
Am I Japanese?

263
00:16:55,953 --> 00:16:57,371
I've been to a lot of countries.

264
00:16:58,205 --> 00:17:00,707
The language and the schools
were always different.

265
00:17:01,250 --> 00:17:04,503
But I've never lived in Japan.

266
00:17:04,586 --> 00:17:06,588
Even so, am I Japanese?

267
00:17:08,382 --> 00:17:11,218
<i>I remember it well.</i>
<i>Because you were such a unique child.</i>

268
00:17:12,386 --> 00:17:14,471
Unique?

269
00:17:14,555 --> 00:17:15,848
Maybe you still are now.

270
00:17:17,474 --> 00:17:18,809
What do you think?

271
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:37,536
Miss Yuka, why did you
choose your current job?

272
00:17:38,871 --> 00:17:42,166
A friend asked me to help out
at an entertainment agency.

273
00:17:43,792 --> 00:17:46,044
That's when I met these boys.

274
00:17:46,628 --> 00:17:49,506
At first, they couldn't
sing or dance well at all.

275
00:17:50,090 --> 00:17:53,677
But as I took care of them,
before I knew it, I became their manager.

276
00:17:55,012 --> 00:17:57,139
I hear they're incredibly popular now.

277
00:17:59,057 --> 00:18:02,394
But perhaps because
they became too popular,

278
00:18:03,312 --> 00:18:04,438
there's been trouble too.

279
00:18:05,939 --> 00:18:08,192
-Trouble?
-Yuki.

280
00:18:08,901 --> 00:18:12,613
-How long are you going to keep talking?
-I'm sorry.

281
00:18:26,501 --> 00:18:28,003
I think by trouble,

282
00:18:28,086 --> 00:18:30,923
she means that concert
in Korea a year ago.

283
00:18:31,006 --> 00:18:32,216
Did something happen?

284
00:18:33,008 --> 00:18:36,803
A lot of stuff happened behind the scenes.
Fans started fighting with each other.

285
00:18:36,887 --> 00:18:38,722
Someone sent a threatening letter.

286
00:18:39,306 --> 00:18:40,307
A threat letter?

287
00:18:40,390 --> 00:18:45,729
"Cancel the concert,
or I'll set fire to the venue."

288
00:18:45,812 --> 00:18:46,855
Whoa…

289
00:18:47,397 --> 00:18:50,651
-What happened?
-Nothing happened,

290
00:18:50,734 --> 00:18:52,027
but they are still wary.

291
00:18:52,611 --> 00:18:57,532
Especially for this concert,
they're all being very careful.

292
00:18:58,408 --> 00:18:59,618
And yet…

293
00:19:02,829 --> 00:19:04,248
What about the passport?

294
00:19:04,915 --> 00:19:06,208
We don't have it yet.

295
00:19:06,291 --> 00:19:10,128
But something's off. With them, as well.

296
00:19:10,963 --> 00:19:14,967
-Do you have, like, a yearbook?
-I threw all that stuff away.

297
00:19:15,050 --> 00:19:17,302
I want to separate myself
from my old self.

298
00:19:17,386 --> 00:19:21,473
So we have nothing
to verify your identity with.

299
00:19:24,685 --> 00:19:28,063
-Oh, this one too?
-This guy is weird too.

300
00:19:28,146 --> 00:19:30,148
He brought over a ton of banned goods.

301
00:19:30,816 --> 00:19:32,276
And he's so confident.

302
00:19:33,568 --> 00:19:36,488
It's almost time for the concert,
but he doesn't look stressed at all.

303
00:19:37,155 --> 00:19:39,700
Yes. That's weird as well.

304
00:19:43,954 --> 00:19:45,539
-Did you just take a photo?
-Huh?

305
00:19:46,123 --> 00:19:47,374
Oh, it's a camera test.

306
00:19:47,457 --> 00:19:49,793
Photography is prohibited here.
Please delete the data too.

307
00:19:51,503 --> 00:19:54,715
-I told you, stop.
-You cannot take photographs.

308
00:19:54,798 --> 00:19:55,966
I'm sorry, sorry, sorry.

309
00:19:58,260 --> 00:19:59,720
Um…

310
00:20:01,430 --> 00:20:04,016
Is that ring an elephant hair ring?

311
00:20:06,143 --> 00:20:08,186
It’s made by weaving hair
from an elephant’s tail.

312
00:20:08,270 --> 00:20:10,689
If it’s real, we need to check it
under CITES.

313
00:20:11,690 --> 00:20:13,275
How much banned stuff are you carrying?

314
00:20:14,818 --> 00:20:18,739
<i>Well, you caught me again. Impressive.</i>

315
00:20:19,948 --> 00:20:21,116
What's with him?

316
00:20:26,621 --> 00:20:29,791
You really do know a lot of things, Mori.

317
00:20:29,875 --> 00:20:31,626
It was an elephant hair ring, right?

318
00:20:32,586 --> 00:20:35,589
I’d seen one before at my previous job.

319
00:20:35,672 --> 00:20:37,090
What was your previous job?

320
00:20:37,674 --> 00:20:38,675
I worked at a museum.

321
00:20:39,634 --> 00:20:41,511
-A museum?
-Yes.

322
00:20:41,595 --> 00:20:44,056
<i>I was in charge</i>
<i>of managing the collection.</i>

323
00:20:44,139 --> 00:20:47,517
<i>I loved being surrounded</i>
<i>by all those objects.</i>

324
00:20:49,644 --> 00:20:53,357
<i>But I used to get scolded a lot too.</i>

325
00:20:54,232 --> 00:20:56,109
This is one of the most

326
00:20:57,194 --> 00:21:00,947
valuable pieces in our collection.

327
00:21:01,615 --> 00:21:03,700
It's an elephant hair ring.

328
00:21:05,952 --> 00:21:08,288
-Please, take a look.
-Um…

329
00:21:10,082 --> 00:21:12,292
That ring may be a fake.

330
00:21:13,293 --> 00:21:15,545
-What?
-If it’s real elephant hair,

331
00:21:15,629 --> 00:21:18,673
each individual strand
should vary in thickness.

332
00:21:18,757 --> 00:21:21,593
But these strands are far too uniform.

333
00:21:23,470 --> 00:21:26,014
The clasp is new too. It’s probably
something made for tourists--

334
00:21:27,849 --> 00:21:30,519
Don't make baseless claims.

335
00:21:31,103 --> 00:21:35,440
You really do have a habit
of meddling, don’t you?

336
00:21:36,650 --> 00:21:37,692
I'm sorry.

337
00:21:39,653 --> 00:21:42,739
I’ve been told that my whole life.

338
00:21:43,865 --> 00:21:45,951
But how did you go from there to customs?

339
00:21:46,743 --> 00:21:48,495
Well…

340
00:21:58,797 --> 00:22:00,257
Got a minute?

341
00:22:05,387 --> 00:22:07,931
Look at that. His sleeve.

342
00:22:11,309 --> 00:22:12,436
Scorch marks?

343
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:16,148
When we got consent
to check his belongings, TDS

344
00:22:16,231 --> 00:22:17,357
detected traces of gunpowder.

345
00:22:18,316 --> 00:22:22,070
-Gunpowder?
-And we found this in his belongings.

346
00:22:24,239 --> 00:22:25,907
A Hi-Fi Unicorn pouch?

347
00:22:26,867 --> 00:22:27,784
This is what was inside.

348
00:22:29,119 --> 00:22:31,496
Gloves, earplugs…

349
00:22:32,581 --> 00:22:36,126
And a floor plan of the concert venue.

350
00:22:37,377 --> 00:22:40,422
-Why did he have something like this?
-He said he didn't know.

351
00:22:40,505 --> 00:22:43,592
But could it be connected
to what Tamai was talking about?

352
00:22:43,675 --> 00:22:46,595
Last year, someone threatened
to burn down the venue, right?

353
00:22:48,180 --> 00:22:49,347
Haoru…

354
00:22:50,974 --> 00:22:54,227
I don't want to suspect him either,
but we can't just ignore this.

355
00:23:03,862 --> 00:23:05,614
Yes, those numbers…

356
00:23:05,697 --> 00:23:07,532
2026…

357
00:23:07,616 --> 00:23:09,284
Could it have something
to do with today's concert?

358
00:23:10,869 --> 00:23:13,496
-Excuse me.
-Ah, hello.

359
00:23:16,082 --> 00:23:17,000
Excuse me.

360
00:23:17,083 --> 00:23:19,544
I am Ikeura, the airport director.

361
00:23:19,628 --> 00:23:22,422
-How did it go?
-Has there been any progress?

362
00:23:22,505 --> 00:23:24,883
We are currently checking
with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

363
00:23:24,966 --> 00:23:28,178
However, we haven't heard back
from the embassy yet.

364
00:23:28,261 --> 00:23:31,514
Regarding the passport,
as of now, there have been no reports

365
00:23:31,598 --> 00:23:33,600
from lost and found or cleaning.

366
00:23:34,559 --> 00:23:36,686
They didn't find my passport?

367
00:23:37,312 --> 00:23:39,022
Let's look one more time.

368
00:23:40,982 --> 00:23:42,150
Right.

369
00:23:42,943 --> 00:23:45,570
Look carefully.

370
00:23:47,822 --> 00:23:50,367
-Search the other side too.
-Let me help you.

371
00:23:50,992 --> 00:23:52,285
-Wait, Mori!
-Don't touch it!

372
00:23:53,870 --> 00:23:54,746
I'm sorry.

373
00:23:55,872 --> 00:23:57,457
-I'm sorry.
-Hey.

374
00:24:01,753 --> 00:24:02,921
Earlier too?

375
00:24:05,090 --> 00:24:06,091
What's this about?

376
00:24:07,008 --> 00:24:08,551
Well…

377
00:24:09,469 --> 00:24:11,846
Mori saw them struggling,
so she just wanted to help.

378
00:24:11,930 --> 00:24:13,932
But that's not part of your job, is it?

379
00:24:14,724 --> 00:24:15,600
No.

380
00:24:17,644 --> 00:24:19,521
I'm very sorry.

381
00:24:19,604 --> 00:24:22,983
A VIP passport is currently missing,

382
00:24:23,066 --> 00:24:27,988
and now an airport staff is going around
touching passengers' stuff.

383
00:24:28,071 --> 00:24:29,489
How do you think that looks?

384
00:24:31,449 --> 00:24:33,785
As I thought, this gate
has far too many problems.

385
00:24:33,868 --> 00:24:36,746
I feel like I've just discovered
part of the reason why.

386
00:24:38,123 --> 00:24:41,084
At this rate, we'll have
to completely reconsider

387
00:24:41,167 --> 00:24:43,586
how this gate is operated, won't we?

388
00:24:46,256 --> 00:24:48,675
Um, um…

389
00:24:48,758 --> 00:24:52,470
-If you want to discuss that, talk to me.
-Counselor…

390
00:24:52,554 --> 00:24:55,890
Our staff caused trouble.
If disciplinary guidance is needed,

391
00:24:55,974 --> 00:24:58,268
-I will handle it later.
-Later?

392
00:24:58,351 --> 00:25:00,729
-The problem is right now--
-Airport Director.

393
00:25:00,812 --> 00:25:02,564
What is the priority issue right now?

394
00:25:02,647 --> 00:25:05,817
-Excuse me?
-Their show is in two hours.

395
00:25:05,900 --> 00:25:08,903
This is no time to be blaming people.

396
00:25:09,821 --> 00:25:11,364
We should look for the passport

397
00:25:11,448 --> 00:25:14,284
and complete all the checks we can, right?

398
00:25:15,744 --> 00:25:18,997
The staff are doing everything
they can right now.

399
00:25:19,080 --> 00:25:20,498
Don't bother them.

400
00:25:21,666 --> 00:25:24,336
Airport Director, let's talk later.

401
00:25:24,419 --> 00:25:26,171
For now, let's keep things moving.

402
00:25:27,714 --> 00:25:30,633
Of course, that's what I was about to say.

403
00:25:30,717 --> 00:25:34,471
I figured as much.
We will keep you updated.

404
00:25:36,139 --> 00:25:39,809
Anyway, just handle this quickly.

405
00:25:43,980 --> 00:25:45,523
Amazing.

406
00:25:46,358 --> 00:25:48,151
She seems different today.

407
00:25:48,234 --> 00:25:49,819
That's true veteran skill.

408
00:25:49,903 --> 00:25:51,946
I think the counselor
is just really angry.

409
00:25:52,030 --> 00:25:55,200
Come on. There's no time
to stand around. Get back to work.

410
00:25:55,283 --> 00:25:56,117
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes.

411
00:26:01,206 --> 00:26:03,291
-Um…
-We'll talk later.

412
00:26:03,375 --> 00:26:04,959
For now, do what you need to do.

413
00:26:06,461 --> 00:26:07,462
Yes, ma'am.

414
00:26:09,964 --> 00:26:11,049
Fukasawa.

415
00:26:13,218 --> 00:26:14,344
Let's go.

416
00:26:21,309 --> 00:26:22,435
Endo.

417
00:26:25,480 --> 00:26:26,356
Look.

418
00:26:27,690 --> 00:26:30,360
We're starting to see his true identity.

419
00:26:32,362 --> 00:26:34,948
This isn't the first time
you brought in contraband, right?

420
00:26:36,157 --> 00:26:37,951
We have a record here.

421
00:26:38,034 --> 00:26:39,244
Liam Lane.

422
00:26:40,370 --> 00:26:41,871
What is the meaning of this?

423
00:26:43,206 --> 00:26:46,376
-You do remember me!
-Huh?

424
00:26:46,459 --> 00:26:50,797
Ever since we met, I haven't
been able to stop thinking about you.

425
00:26:51,923 --> 00:26:53,299
I'm so happy to see you again.

426
00:26:56,678 --> 00:26:58,388
Then what about the Hi-Fi concert?

427
00:26:58,471 --> 00:27:00,765
No, I'm not going.

428
00:27:00,849 --> 00:27:03,893
I just thought this pouch
would make me look like a fan.

429
00:27:04,519 --> 00:27:07,981
-Look like a fan?
-I wanted you to catch me again.

430
00:27:08,064 --> 00:27:14,112
It's my way of showing my devotion.

431
00:27:17,240 --> 00:27:18,241
Here.

432
00:27:23,079 --> 00:27:26,124
All right then, I will hold onto this
as an item subject to inspection.

433
00:27:26,207 --> 00:27:27,041
What?

434
00:27:27,917 --> 00:27:31,296
Also, it seems the purpose of your entry
differs from what you declared,

435
00:27:31,379 --> 00:27:33,131
so Immigration will take care of you.

436
00:27:33,882 --> 00:27:37,927
-Wait…
-Think about the rules more, and me less.

437
00:27:48,062 --> 00:27:52,400
So, if this means the year 2026,
what about the rest?

438
00:27:52,484 --> 00:27:55,153
2029? That's too far into the future.

439
00:27:56,196 --> 00:27:58,781
Skip the rehearsal.
Make sure wardrobe is ready.

440
00:27:58,865 --> 00:28:01,284
We'll still barely make 18…

441
00:28:02,243 --> 00:28:03,745
Six p.m…

442
00:28:10,043 --> 00:28:11,127
Um…

443
00:28:13,087 --> 00:28:15,298
Could this be referring to time?

444
00:28:15,381 --> 00:28:18,718
-Time?
-It's not the year 2026.

445
00:28:18,801 --> 00:28:20,762
It's 20:26, or 8:26 p.m.

446
00:28:21,971 --> 00:28:24,807
8:26 p.m…

447
00:28:25,433 --> 00:28:29,062
What do these 3R, 4B, and 5G mean then?

448
00:28:30,563 --> 00:28:32,815
8:30. I won't be able to make it…

449
00:28:34,943 --> 00:28:38,738
What if they're colors?
R for red, B for blue,

450
00:28:38,822 --> 00:28:40,198
G for gold?

451
00:28:41,115 --> 00:28:43,576
So then, in other words, it means…

452
00:28:43,660 --> 00:28:44,702
Fireworks!

453
00:28:44,786 --> 00:28:47,914
Tamai said fireworks
would go off at the venue at 8:30.

454
00:28:50,416 --> 00:28:51,918
Fireworks…

455
00:28:55,672 --> 00:28:57,257
Haoru, you are…

456
00:28:57,340 --> 00:28:58,550
Fireworks…

457
00:28:59,759 --> 00:29:00,844
I remember.

458
00:29:02,428 --> 00:29:04,764
I'm a pyrotechnician.

459
00:29:04,848 --> 00:29:06,766
My son is a pyrotechnician too.

460
00:29:07,392 --> 00:29:11,855
I came here today to see his fireworks.

461
00:29:16,025 --> 00:29:18,486
This is from him.

462
00:29:18,570 --> 00:29:21,698
-So his son is doing our fireworks?
-Fireworks, huh?

463
00:29:21,781 --> 00:29:24,242
-I'm looking forward to that.
-Yes, me too.

464
00:29:24,325 --> 00:29:27,370
-Thank you.
-Ah, thank goodness.

465
00:29:28,204 --> 00:29:30,665
‎But, where were all of you…

466
00:29:30,748 --> 00:29:34,878
Regarding the passport,
it wasn't in Haoru's luggage.

467
00:29:34,961 --> 00:29:37,547
It wasn't in Liam's luggage either.

468
00:29:38,840 --> 00:29:41,926
Which leaves only one person.

469
00:29:44,178 --> 00:29:46,306
This way, please. I'll take your luggage.

470
00:29:48,266 --> 00:29:49,517
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

471
00:29:56,232 --> 00:29:59,736
Ma'am! Ma'am, ma'am. Please calm down.

472
00:29:59,819 --> 00:30:02,155
-Why?
-You have to wait.

473
00:30:02,238 --> 00:30:03,615
Do you have a minute?

474
00:30:04,532 --> 00:30:08,286
I looked into the fight last year again
and found a video.

475
00:30:14,167 --> 00:30:16,044
What?

476
00:30:16,127 --> 00:30:18,504
No!

477
00:30:22,759 --> 00:30:25,887
Stop filming!

478
00:30:25,970 --> 00:30:27,472
That person!

479
00:30:27,555 --> 00:30:28,723
Stop filming!

480
00:30:30,642 --> 00:30:33,186
Mira, this is you, right?

481
00:30:34,896 --> 00:30:38,733
Around this time, a letter arrived
at Hi-Fi Unicorn's agency saying that

482
00:30:39,442 --> 00:30:42,570
if they didn't cancel the concert,
someone would set fire to the venue.

483
00:30:45,865 --> 00:30:47,450
Are you saying I did that?

484
00:30:48,409 --> 00:30:51,329
If you know anything,
could you please tell us?

485
00:30:53,039 --> 00:30:54,123
You wouldn't believe me.

486
00:30:55,124 --> 00:30:57,669
Wait a minute. Mira,

487
00:30:58,252 --> 00:31:01,089
rather than fighting, it looks like
you're trying to grab her phone.

488
00:31:02,924 --> 00:31:04,133
You're right.

489
00:31:04,217 --> 00:31:06,886
Even though there were two of them,
she didn't back down.

490
00:31:09,681 --> 00:31:12,934
There must have been a reason
for you to go that far, right?

491
00:31:14,519 --> 00:31:16,354
They were the ones who sent the letter.

492
00:31:17,605 --> 00:31:21,067
Those two caused trouble before
and were banned.

493
00:31:22,360 --> 00:31:23,945
Troublesome people, huh?

494
00:31:24,779 --> 00:31:26,698
I tracked them down and warned them,

495
00:31:26,781 --> 00:31:28,658
but then they beat me up.

496
00:31:28,741 --> 00:31:30,910
So that's what caused that commotion.

497
00:31:31,911 --> 00:31:35,123
Are you saying some radical fans did it?

498
00:31:35,206 --> 00:31:36,833
Don't call them fans.

499
00:31:36,916 --> 00:31:39,419
Real fans would never
cause trouble for their idols.

500
00:31:40,003 --> 00:31:43,673
I made them promise never
to involve themselves with Hi-Fi again.

501
00:31:44,340 --> 00:31:47,051
-Oh my.
-She's a model fan.

502
00:31:47,135 --> 00:31:49,178
So, the reason you had
plastic surgery was…

503
00:31:49,262 --> 00:31:52,056
My face was beaten black and blue.

504
00:31:52,140 --> 00:31:53,850
I got settlement money,
so it was done in no time at all.

505
00:31:53,933 --> 00:31:55,727
No time at all…

506
00:31:55,810 --> 00:31:58,771
Well, the police gave me
quite a scolding, though.

507
00:31:59,897 --> 00:32:00,898
The police?

508
00:32:02,817 --> 00:32:04,861
Hey, huh?

509
00:32:04,944 --> 00:32:05,778
TAKAYA IUCHI
INTERNATIONAL CRIMES DETECTIVE

510
00:32:05,862 --> 00:32:06,863
Oh, Chika.

511
00:32:07,822 --> 00:32:12,201
Hey, we looked into it for you.
Stop treating us like your handymen.

512
00:32:12,285 --> 00:32:14,704
-That's a huge help.
-Like I said, we're not your handymen.

513
00:32:16,497 --> 00:32:17,832
I mean, am I right?

514
00:32:17,915 --> 00:32:21,002
Mira Tono, we found
your records from that incident.

515
00:32:22,962 --> 00:32:25,423
Perfect! With this,
we can perform a match!

516
00:32:26,090 --> 00:32:28,134
-Does that mean I…
-You should be able to enter.

517
00:32:28,217 --> 00:32:29,177
Really?

518
00:32:29,260 --> 00:32:31,971
Thank goodness.
Now you can go to the concert.

519
00:32:37,143 --> 00:32:38,394
She's holding something back.

520
00:32:39,437 --> 00:32:42,523
-Is something wrong?
-I'm so glad, but

521
00:32:42,607 --> 00:32:44,901
as a fan, I'm worried.

522
00:32:44,984 --> 00:32:48,071
-I don't know if Hi-Fi will be okay.
-I get it.

523
00:32:48,905 --> 00:32:50,239
What do you get?

524
00:32:57,914 --> 00:32:58,998
We can't wait any more.

525
00:32:59,082 --> 00:33:01,125
We'll do this concert with four people.

526
00:33:01,209 --> 00:33:02,794
Let's go.

527
00:33:06,798 --> 00:33:07,757
Excuse me.

528
00:33:11,260 --> 00:33:13,888
-Miss Yuki.
-Did you find the passport?

529
00:33:13,971 --> 00:33:15,515
No, not yet.

530
00:33:16,724 --> 00:33:17,767
I see.

531
00:33:18,810 --> 00:33:22,605
But, you know, right, Miss Yuki?

532
00:33:23,731 --> 00:33:25,691
You know where the passport is, don't you?

533
00:33:27,276 --> 00:33:29,278
Yuki does?

534
00:33:29,362 --> 00:33:30,279
What are you talking about?

535
00:33:30,363 --> 00:33:34,158
Hi-Fi Unicorn has had an especially
tough schedule recently, right?

536
00:33:34,951 --> 00:33:37,036
Touring all over the world,

537
00:33:37,120 --> 00:33:40,248
then doing a concert
in Japan the day they arrive.

538
00:33:40,331 --> 00:33:41,791
The fans are very worried.

539
00:33:43,376 --> 00:33:47,338
In particular, Hyeongyul
wasn't feeling well.

540
00:33:47,421 --> 00:33:51,300
As the person closest to him,
you must have known that, Yuki.

541
00:33:53,052 --> 00:33:54,595
So what?

542
00:33:54,679 --> 00:33:56,973
Why does that mean
I'm the one holding the passport?

543
00:33:58,933 --> 00:34:00,393
I found it strange.

544
00:34:03,146 --> 00:34:04,647
That pouch of yours, Miss Yuki.

545
00:34:08,317 --> 00:34:11,362
Everyone else checked their bags
over and over again,

546
00:34:11,445 --> 00:34:13,614
trying to find the passport.

547
00:34:14,365 --> 00:34:20,997
But you haven't opened
that pouch even once.

548
00:34:21,956 --> 00:34:23,332
-I did open it.
-No, you didn't.

549
00:34:23,416 --> 00:34:24,458
I did.

550
00:34:25,376 --> 00:34:26,711
You just didn't see me do it.

551
00:34:26,794 --> 00:34:28,880
Yes, I didn't.

552
00:34:30,464 --> 00:34:34,302
But the object itself
says you haven't opened it.

553
00:34:41,392 --> 00:34:42,310
This says it.

554
00:34:48,024 --> 00:34:49,275
A thread?

555
00:34:49,358 --> 00:34:51,736
That piece of thread has been stuck there

556
00:34:51,819 --> 00:34:53,905
the whole time since you arrived.

557
00:34:58,117 --> 00:35:01,037
If you unzipped it,
the thread should have fallen off.

558
00:35:01,120 --> 00:35:02,538
But it’s still there.

559
00:35:07,251 --> 00:35:08,336
I'm sorry.

560
00:35:09,170 --> 00:35:11,547
It’s been bothering me the whole time.

561
00:35:12,465 --> 00:35:16,552
But I was afraid you’d get mad
if I touched your things without asking.

562
00:35:17,887 --> 00:35:21,098
-Yuki, you…
-Yuki…

563
00:35:25,186 --> 00:35:28,105
The first kid I was in charge of…

564
00:35:28,689 --> 00:35:31,734
She loved singing,
worked so desperately hard,

565
00:35:32,818 --> 00:35:35,154
and pushed herself
to the absolute limit for her fans.

566
00:35:36,656 --> 00:35:41,410
But she pushed herself too far
and ruined her health.

567
00:35:43,788 --> 00:35:46,958
I never wanted to let anyone
go through that again.

568
00:35:50,503 --> 00:35:53,422
I knew Hyeongyul was at his limit.

569
00:35:58,970 --> 00:36:01,180
-Are you okay?
-Yes, I'm fine.

570
00:36:01,264 --> 00:36:05,935
<i>But when I thought of the fans waiting</i>
<i>for the concert, I couldn't say anything.</i>

571
00:36:07,812 --> 00:36:08,813
<i>And then, on impulse…</i>

572
00:36:08,896 --> 00:36:09,814
Are you ok?

573
00:36:11,691 --> 00:36:14,277
-Hey, hurry up.
-Coming.

574
00:36:16,445 --> 00:36:19,907
<i>I just wanted him to rest,</i>
<i>even for a little bit.</i>

575
00:36:20,992 --> 00:36:22,326
That's why…

576
00:36:33,337 --> 00:36:34,171
Yuki…

577
00:36:34,880 --> 00:36:38,843
This was the only way you could give
Hyeongyul a break, right?

578
00:36:40,803 --> 00:36:44,598
I'm very sorry.
I intend to take full responsibility.

579
00:36:46,225 --> 00:36:47,476
Miss Yuki?

580
00:36:48,436 --> 00:36:49,603
What responsibility?

581
00:36:50,938 --> 00:36:54,191
You were worried about us, right?
We're okay now.

582
00:36:54,275 --> 00:36:56,235
-Right?
-Yes.

583
00:36:56,986 --> 00:37:00,239
I got some medicine from the doctor,
so I feel much better now.

584
00:37:00,323 --> 00:37:03,117
It's been a while since
we've had time to relax like this.

585
00:37:03,200 --> 00:37:05,828
Thanks to that,
my energy is fully recharged!

586
00:37:05,911 --> 00:37:07,955
I want to go see our fans, now!

587
00:37:08,039 --> 00:37:09,999
Right, let's hurry.

588
00:37:10,082 --> 00:37:12,043
What a relief.
Let's only think about the performance.

589
00:37:13,294 --> 00:37:14,378
President.

590
00:37:15,338 --> 00:37:16,714
I just remembered.

591
00:37:16,797 --> 00:37:20,092
I was the one who told you
to hold onto Hyeongyul's passport.

592
00:37:23,637 --> 00:37:26,432
Guys. Hurry up. We're going.

593
00:37:26,515 --> 00:37:27,350
-Yes, sir!
-Yes, sir!

594
00:37:27,433 --> 00:37:29,935
-We're all going together.
-Yes!

595
00:37:32,146 --> 00:37:33,272
Nice!

596
00:37:34,732 --> 00:37:37,443
-Thank you too.
-What?

597
00:37:37,526 --> 00:37:39,945
You were concerned
about my health, weren't you?

598
00:37:40,738 --> 00:37:41,947
How did you figure it out?

599
00:37:43,699 --> 00:37:44,825
Well…

600
00:37:45,701 --> 00:37:47,870
Mori, stop that already.

601
00:37:54,043 --> 00:37:57,129
I saw an empty sheet of fever medicine.

602
00:37:57,963 --> 00:38:00,758
So I realized you must have had a fever.

603
00:38:02,968 --> 00:38:05,805
I did something unnecessary again.

604
00:38:07,348 --> 00:38:09,141
It wasn't unnecessary at all.

605
00:38:11,102 --> 00:38:12,478
Thank you.

606
00:38:12,561 --> 00:38:14,563
He's important to us,
and you looked after him.

607
00:38:15,189 --> 00:38:16,982
You're a wonderful customs officer.

608
00:38:18,901 --> 00:38:21,904
Thank you very much! All right, let's go!

609
00:38:28,536 --> 00:38:29,995
Welcome to Japan.

610
00:38:32,498 --> 00:38:34,959
Everyone, thank you very much.

611
00:38:35,042 --> 00:38:37,545
-Thank you!
-Thank you.

612
00:38:39,797 --> 00:38:41,715
Welcome to Japan.

613
00:38:43,384 --> 00:38:44,635
Let's move.

614
00:38:44,718 --> 00:38:45,761
Yeah, let's go.

615
00:38:50,766 --> 00:38:54,186
-Looks like they'll make it.
-Yes.

616
00:38:55,438 --> 00:38:59,900
However, I do expect
an explanation. A lengthy one.

617
00:38:59,984 --> 00:39:01,193
-What?
-Yes.

618
00:39:02,111 --> 00:39:04,363
Let's go, shall we, Counselor?

619
00:39:04,447 --> 00:39:08,659
Ah, no, please go ahead first.

620
00:39:16,625 --> 00:39:17,960
You've gotta be kidding me.

621
00:39:19,879 --> 00:39:21,380
My shift was over long ago.

622
00:39:22,339 --> 00:39:23,716
You've gotta be kidding me!

623
00:39:34,101 --> 00:39:35,978
They're doing it!

624
00:39:36,061 --> 00:39:37,897
‎That's amazing!

625
00:39:37,980 --> 00:39:40,524
Seems like the Hi-Fi concert
is going well.

626
00:39:40,608 --> 00:39:42,276
I wonder if Haoru's watching.

627
00:39:43,611 --> 00:39:45,946
Tamai, you couldn't get
an autograph or handshake, huh.

628
00:39:46,030 --> 00:39:47,656
Well, it's just as good.

629
00:39:47,740 --> 00:39:51,869
Idols are idols, work is work.
I'm satisfied with this.

630
00:39:52,661 --> 00:39:53,954
That's brilliant.

631
00:39:54,038 --> 00:39:55,581
‎You're too close.

632
00:39:56,415 --> 00:39:58,542
Do you have an idol you support, Mori?

633
00:39:59,418 --> 00:40:00,586
Idols?

634
00:40:01,420 --> 00:40:05,174
Just having someone like that is enough
to give people the courage to go on.

635
00:40:05,257 --> 00:40:07,009
It gives them vitality in their life.

636
00:40:07,927 --> 00:40:11,555
-I guess you wouldn't get it, Mori.
-She doesn't even know Hi-Fi.

637
00:40:13,140 --> 00:40:14,850
I do understand having someone like that.

638
00:40:16,810 --> 00:40:19,104
Who is your idol in Hi-Fi, Tamai?

639
00:40:20,022 --> 00:40:22,441
-All of them.
-All of them!

640
00:40:22,525 --> 00:40:23,859
Come on. Who is it?

641
00:40:24,568 --> 00:40:28,155
-Me?
-Good work, everyone.

642
00:40:28,239 --> 00:40:30,491
-Mr. Fukasawa!
-Counselor, you too!

643
00:40:30,574 --> 00:40:32,868
Good work, everybody.

644
00:40:33,994 --> 00:40:35,955
How did things go
with the airport director?

645
00:40:36,038 --> 00:40:37,623
We really got chewed out.

646
00:40:37,706 --> 00:40:41,627
He said Gate 24 caused
one problem after another.

647
00:40:42,419 --> 00:40:43,462
I figured he'd say that.

648
00:40:44,880 --> 00:40:45,798
I'm sorry.

649
00:40:47,925 --> 00:40:50,636
What are you sorry for?

650
00:40:52,388 --> 00:40:55,975
Problems occur everywhere, all the time.

651
00:40:57,518 --> 00:41:01,438
It just means our gate
discovers those problems first.

652
00:41:03,274 --> 00:41:06,026
Before those problems get
brought into the country,

653
00:41:07,194 --> 00:41:10,739
you all notice them
and stop them right at the border

654
00:41:12,199 --> 00:41:15,286
That's why I am proud of our gate

655
00:41:16,704 --> 00:41:18,330
and how problematic we are.

656
00:41:22,710 --> 00:41:24,420
With that being said,

657
00:41:25,045 --> 00:41:27,423
peace and quiet is best.

658
00:41:27,506 --> 00:41:28,591
That's true.

659
00:41:31,552 --> 00:41:33,554
I think so too!

660
00:41:34,263 --> 00:41:37,641
Man, another exhausting day!

661
00:41:38,392 --> 00:41:39,476
Good work!

662
00:41:40,603 --> 00:41:43,147
-All right!
-Have a seat.

663
00:41:57,620 --> 00:42:00,289
"You really do have a
habit of meddling, don’t you?"

664
00:42:03,626 --> 00:42:04,585
I'm sorry.

665
00:42:06,587 --> 00:42:08,881
I, uh, apologize.

666
00:42:08,964 --> 00:42:14,261
She gets, uh, too particular about stuff.

667
00:42:14,345 --> 00:42:17,556
What's wrong with that?

668
00:42:21,310 --> 00:42:24,980
It's her job to be particular, isn't it?

669
00:42:25,064 --> 00:42:27,941
Which makes it a wonderful thing.

670
00:42:29,401 --> 00:42:34,031
This museum has
many things that hold value.

671
00:42:35,783 --> 00:42:39,244
A person like you holds a lot of value.

672
00:42:41,288 --> 00:42:45,751
I'd love for someone
like you to be on our team.

673
00:42:47,961 --> 00:42:50,172
Thank you very much for today.

674
00:42:52,675 --> 00:42:58,097
I intend to reform Japan's border control.

675
00:42:58,180 --> 00:43:02,601
Someday, I will create the strongest gate
to protect this country.

676
00:43:35,050 --> 00:43:38,887
MIDORI SUGIHARA

677
00:43:44,601 --> 00:43:46,061
-What's wrong?
-Nothing.

678
00:43:52,109 --> 00:43:54,570
-May I have one?
-Yes.

679
00:44:01,326 --> 00:44:02,202
It's delicious.

680
00:44:23,390 --> 00:44:25,184
‎She was murdered.

681
00:44:25,267 --> 00:44:26,935
<i>‎This was on the victim's smartphone.</i>

682
00:44:27,019 --> 00:44:29,313
‎You knew the victim well beforehand,
‎didn't you?

683
00:44:29,396 --> 00:44:32,816
‎It looks like she chose Matsuyama
‎as her customs officer.

684
00:44:32,900 --> 00:44:34,067
‎We want to know the truth.

685
00:44:34,151 --> 00:44:35,027
‎The truth?

686
00:44:35,110 --> 00:44:37,780
‎He submitted his resignation.

687
00:44:37,863 --> 00:44:38,697
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman

